Cores          : carry_forward_rounding_pkg, donor_limit_pkg

                 ⚠ SCOPE of donor_limit_pkg, narrower than upstream. The multiplier
                 Mrl is held in hundredths and the share in whole percent; upstream
                 uses doubles, ceil(), and a tolerance comparison (EIM_DBL_LT) that
                 this core replaces with exact integer comparison. The "unset"
                 sentinel -1 is modelled as a Boolean flag. INT_MAX becomes the
                 subtype's last value. Counts are capped at 30000 so every product
                 in a contract stays in range. EI_CountDonorsReachedDonorLimit is
                 not modelled.

                 What is proved: the rounded-up ratio is exactly the least count
                 whose multiple by the donors reaches the recipients (and likewise
                 for the scaled ceiling); the limit is at least one, at least the
                 fixed count when set, and at least the scaled ceiling when a
                 multiplier is set; when the multiplier is at least 1.00 the limit
                 is at least the rounded-up ratio, so the donors together cover
                 every recipient; and one more non-recipient respondent never
                 turns "enough donors" into "not enough". The two ceiling
                 characterisations and the monotonicity theorem carry the weight;
                 Donor_Limit's own bounds follow from Integer'Max.

